 "result_text": "`create-pr` fails without a token because creating a PR is a `POST` to `/pulls`, and GitHub requires authentication for that. Reading `/pulls` in a browser is a `GET`, which works for public repos without a token. For an unauthenticated `POST`, GitHub answers 404 instead of 401, which is why the old error looked so odd. I haven't run the tests or tried the new message against the real API.\n\nThe fix is a better error message for 404 responses in `git_machete/github.py`:\n\n- **No token found:** the message now says the request got a 404, that authentication may be needed, and lists where a token can be provided (`GITHUB_TOKEN`, `~/.github-token`, `gh`, `hub`). It also links to the page for generating one.\n- **Token present:** the message says the endpoint may not exist or the token (possibly expired or lacking `repo` access) may not allow access.\n\nI left the unauthenticated `GET` behaviour alone, since public repos already work for those.",
